  Kernels are SLOWER by 206.075x.

  Attribution: 169 NKI launches/step, delta 8831 ms
    => 52.3 ms of added cost per NKI call
    host dispatch alone (Finding #19, ~0.36 ms/call) = ~61 ms
    52.3 ms/call is 145x host dispatch, so this is
    NOT launch-bound. Something structural is costing per-call time —
    most likely each @nki.jit call executing as its own NEFF with an HBM
    round trip, rather than fusing into the surrounding XLA graph.
    Re-run with --only to attribute the cost to a specific kernel.

  Caveats: forward-only; single logical core; eager (not torch.compile);
  kernelized via kernelize_for_neuron() since use_kernels=True can't route
  to Neuron; attention FLOPs counted without a causal-mask discount.
